### GameVault API — Demo Requests
### Requires the "REST Client" extension in VS Code (search "REST Client" by
### Huachao Mao in the Extensions panel, install, reload if asked).
### Usage: click the "Send Request" link that appears above each ### block.
### Make sure `npm run dev` is running first.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api

### =========================================================
### 1. CRUD Operations — Players
### =========================================================

### Create a player
POST {{baseUrl}}/players
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "demoPlayer2",
  "email": "demoplayer@gamevault2.gg",
  "role": "Duelist",
  "country": "US"
}

### List players (also demonstrates #5 Pagination and Sorting)
GET {{baseUrl}}/players?page=1&limit=10&sort=username

### Get a single player by ID (replace with a real _id from the list above)
GET {{baseUrl}}/players/6aae2a3c29fcbeb2aeab1d9b

### Update a player
PUT {{baseUrl}}/players/6aae2a3c29fcbeb2aeab1d9a
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role": "IGL"
}

### Delete a player
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/players/PASTE_PLAYER_ID_HERE


### =========================================================
### 2. Relational Linking — Teams (roster is an array of Player refs)
### =========================================================

### List teams — note each team's "players" array is populated with real
### player documents (username, role), not just raw ObjectIds
GET {{baseUrl}}/teams

### Get a single team, roster + captain populated
GET {{baseUrl}}/teams/6aae2a3c29fcbeb2aeab1d98


### =========================================================
### 3. Aggregation Pipeline — Stats
### =========================================================

### Team rankings: win rate + roster size computed in the database via $lookup
GET {{baseUrl}}/stats/rankings

### Same, filtered to one game
GET {{baseUrl}}/stats/rankings?game=Valorant

### Match volume/outcomes grouped by game
GET {{baseUrl}}/stats/games-breakdown


### =========================================================
### 4. Indexing — no dedicated endpoint; show this in MongoDB Atlas/Compass
### instead: MongoDB Atlas > Clusters > Browse collections > click arrow next to gamevault > tournaments > Indexes tab, point out the
### `location_2dsphere` and text indexes, and `teams`/`players` schema files
### in the code (src/models/*.js) showing schema.index(...) calls.
### =========================================================


### =========================================================
### 5. Pagination & Sorting - Every list endpoint takes page, limit, sort — response includes total and pages so a frontend can build page controls
### =========================================================


### =========================================================
### 6. Text Search — Tournaments
### =========================================================

GET {{baseUrl}}/tournaments/search?q=invitational


### =========================================================
### 7. Multi-Document ACID Transactions — Roster Transfer
### =========================================================

### Moves a player from their current team (if any) onto a new team.
### Both the Player document and both Team documents are updated together,
### inside a single MongoDB transaction (session.withTransaction in
### src/controllers/teamController.js).
POST {{baseUrl}}/teams/transfer
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "playerId": "6aae2ac3eae1a2dfeafc926a",
  "toTeamId": "6aae2a3c29fcbeb2aeab1d96"
}


### =========================================================
### 8. TTL Index — Match Invites (auto-delete after 24h)
### =========================================================

### Create an invite — point out the `createdAt` TTL index in
### src/models/MatchInvite.js (expires: 86400). In a real demo you can't wait
### 24h, so just show the document exists now, then show the schema code.
POST {{baseUrl}}/invites
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fromTeam": "6aae2a3c29fcbeb2aeab1d96",
  "toTeam": "6aae2a3c29fcbeb2aeab1d98",
  "message": "Scrim before the qualifier?"
}

### List invites
GET {{baseUrl}}/invites


### =========================================================
### 9. Geospatial Queries — Nearby LAN Tournaments
### =========================================================

GET {{baseUrl}}/tournaments/nearby?lng=-122.42&lat=37.77&maxDistance=100000


### =========================================================
### 10. Change Streams — Live Match Score
### =========================================================
### DO NOT use REST Client's "Send Request" for the stream itself — it's not
### built for long-lived streaming responses. Instead:
###
### 1. Split the VS Code terminal (icon at top-right of the terminal panel)
###    to open a SECOND terminal next to the one running `npm run dev`.
### 2. In that new terminal, run:
###      curl.exe -N http://localhost:5000/api/matches/live/stream
###    It prints ": connected" and then waits — that's correct.
### 3. First get a real match ID with the GET request below (Send Request),
###    copy its "_id", paste it into the PATCH request's URL below.
### 4. Click "Send Request" on the PATCH request.
### 5. Look back at the terminal from step 2 — a new JSON line should appear
###    immediately, showing the change event live.

### Get a real match ID first
GET {{baseUrl}}/matches

### Trigger the score update (this is what the curl terminal will observe)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/matches/PASTE_MATCH_ID_HERE/score
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "scoreA": 2,
  "scoreB": 1,
  "status": "Live"
}


### =========================================================
### 11. Faceted Search ($facet & $bucket) — Multi-Dimensional Analytics
### =========================================================
### Computes 4 parallel analytics pipelines in a single database roundtrip:
### 1) Prize pool buckets ($0-$5k, $5k-$25k, $25k-$100k) via $bucket
### 2) Tournament game breakdown via $sortByCount
### 3) Tournament status distribution
### 4) Top 3 highest prize tournaments
GET {{baseUrl}}/stats/tournaments/faceted


### =========================================================
### 12. Recursive Graph Traversal ($graphLookup) — Tournament Bracket Tree
### =========================================================
### Traces the entire tournament bracket dependency tree backwards starting
### from the Championship Final match down to Semifinals and Quarterfinals.
### First run GET /tournaments, copy the _id of "GameVault Winter Championship"
GET {{baseUrl}}/tournaments

### Get the complete recursive bracket progression tree
GET {{baseUrl}}/tournaments/PASTE_TOURNAMENT_ID_HERE/bracket-tree


### =========================================================
### 13. Capped Collection (capped: true) — Circular Match Event Ticker
### =========================================================
### Fixed-size collection acting as a high-speed circular FIFO buffer.
### When full, oldest entries are automatically purged by MongoDB with zero cron jobs.

### Log a real-time event to the capped collection
POST {{baseUrl}}/audit/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventType": "Kill",
  "message": "v1per secured an ace (5 kills) on Ascent B-site!",
  "severity": "Info"
}

### Read the latest events in natural FIFO insertion order ($natural: -1)
GET {{baseUrl}}/audit/events?limit=10


### =========================================================
### 14. Engine Schema Validation ($jsonSchema) — Native DB Constraints
### =========================================================
### Enforced directly by the MongoDB core storage engine (code 121),
### rejecting writes that violate business rules even if application code is bypassed.

### Valid contract: succeeds (salary >= 500, regex CTR-####-XX matches)
### (Get a real player ID and team ID from GET /players and GET /teams)
POST {{baseUrl}}/contracts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "player": "PASTE_PLAYER_ID_HERE",
  "team": "PASTE_TEAM_ID_HERE",
  "contractCode": "CTR-3030-NA",
  "salary": 2500,
  "status": "Active"
}

### Invalid contract test: demonstrates MongoDB engine rejection!
### (salary is 200 which is < 500 minimum; contract code does not match regex)
### Observe the database returns validation error code 121!
POST {{baseUrl}}/contracts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "player": "PASTE_PLAYER_ID_HERE",
  "team": "PASTE_TEAM_ID_HERE",
  "contractCode": "INVALID_CODE",
  "salary": 200,
  "status": "Active"
}

### List contracts
GET {{baseUrl}}/contracts


### =========================================================
### 15. Partial Filter Index (partialFilterExpression) — Free Agents
### =========================================================
### Only indexes the small fraction of players where team == null.
### Drastically saves memory & index writes compared to indexing all players.
GET {{baseUrl}}/players/free-agents


### =========================================================
### 16. Positional Array Updates (arrayFilters & $inc) — Pinpoint Stat Updates
### =========================================================
### Atomically increments a specific player's kills inside the match's
### playerPerformances array in-place, preventing race conditions.
### Copy a match _id from GET /matches and a player _id from GET /players
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/matches/PASTE_MATCH_ID_HERE/player-stats
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "playerId": "PASTE_PLAYER_ID_HERE",
  "killsDelta": 3,
  "deathsDelta": 1,
  "assistsDelta": 2
}


### =========================================================
### 17. Soft Delete & Query Lifecycle Hooks (pre('find'))
### =========================================================
### Soft deletes a team by marking isDeleted: true. The Mongoose pre('find')
### middleware hook automatically hides it from normal queries while preserving
### historical tournament records. Can be restored anytime.

### 1) Soft-delete a team (copy team ID from GET /teams)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/teams/PASTE_TEAM_ID_HERE/soft

### 2) Notice the team has disappeared from the normal list
GET {{baseUrl}}/teams

### 3) Query with includeDeleted=true (admin view) to see it in the recycle bin
GET {{baseUrl}}/teams?includeDeleted=true

### 4) Restore the team back to active status
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/teams/PASTE_TEAM_ID_HERE/restore


### =========================================================
### 18. Bulk Write Operations (bulkWrite) — Batch Match Reporter
### =========================================================
### Bundles multiple match score updates into a single database network roundtrip.
### Copy two real match IDs from GET /matches
POST {{baseUrl}}/matches/bulk-results
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "updates": [
    {
      "matchId": "PASTE_FIRST_MATCH_ID_HERE",
      "scoreA": 3,
      "scoreB": 1,
      "status": "Completed"
    },
    {
      "matchId": "PASTE_SECOND_MATCH_ID_HERE",
      "scoreA": 2,
      "scoreB": 2,
      "status": "Completed"
    }
  ]
}


### =========================================================
### 19. Collation (strength: 2) — Case-Insensitive GamerTag Matching
### =========================================================
### Matches gamerTag regardless of casing ('v1per', 'V1PER', 'V1per')
### using index collation { locale: 'en', strength: 2 } without regex scans.

### Search with uppercase
GET {{baseUrl}}/players/lookup/tag?handle=V1PER

### Search with lowercase (returns the exact same player)
GET {{baseUrl}}/players/lookup/tag?handle=v1per


### =========================================================
### 20. GridFS Chunked Binary Storage (GridFSBucket) — Rulebooks & Replays
### =========================================================
### Slices large files into 255KB chunks stored in media.files and media.chunks.

### List files currently stored in MongoDB GridFS
GET {{baseUrl}}/media

### Stream the rulebook PDF chunks directly to client
### (Replace ID with the _id from the list above)
GET {{baseUrl}}/media/PASTE_MEDIA_ID_HERE/stream

